{number: 91}
{title: Jesus, Lover of My Soul}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] Jesus, Lover [F] of my [C] soul,
Let me to Thy [G7] bosom [C] fly,
While the nearer [F] waters [C] roll,
While the tempest [G7] still is [C] high:
Hide me, O my [F] Savior, [C] hide,
Till the storm of [G7] life is [C] past;
Safe into the [F] haven [C] guide;
O re-[G7] ceive my soul at [C] last.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] Other refuge [F] have I [C] none;
Hangs my helpless [G7] soul on [C] Thee;
Leave, ah! leave me [F] not a-[C] lone,
Still support and [G7] comfort [C] me.
All my trust on [F] Thee is [C] stayed,
All my help from [G7] Thee I [C] bring;
Cover my de-[F] fenseless [C] head
With the [G7] shadow of Thy [C] wing.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C] Plenteous grace with [F] Thee is [C] found,
Grace to cover [G7] all my [C] sin;
Let the healing [F] streams a-[C] bound;
Make and keep me [G7] pure with-[C] in.
Thou of life the [F] Fountain [C] art,
Freely let me [G7] take of [C] Thee;
Spring Thou up with-[F] in my [C] heart;
Rise to [G7] all eterni-[C] ty.
{end_of_verse}
